From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Umair Ahmed Shah <umairahmedshah@hotmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: monaco-monza-som: add the SerDes 0.9 V
 supply

The SGMII SerDes PHY is powered by a 0.9 V and a 1.2 V rail. The Monza
SoM describes only the 1.2 V one (phy-supply = vreg_l5a), so the driver
falls back to a dummy regulator for vdda-0p9 and nothing votes for
vreg_l4a on behalf of the SerDes. Whenever no other consumer holds that
rail, SerDes calibration fails on interface open:

  qcom-dwmac-sgmii-phy 8909000.phy: QSERDES_COM_C_READY_STATUS timed-out
  qcom-ethqos 23040000.ethernet eth0: __stmmac_open: Serdes powerup failed

Add vdda-0p9-supply = vreg_l4a, the 0.9 V rail the QCS8300 Ride and
Monaco EVK use for the same PHY. phy-supply stays: the qcom-6.18.y
driver requests only vdda-0p9 by name and relies on the PHY core's
phy-supply vote for the 1.2 V rail. Mainline's two-supply driver
(vdda-0p9 and vdda-1p2, phy-supply deprecated) needs the upstream form
of this change instead.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Assisted-by: claude-code:claude-opus-5-5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco-monza-som.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco-monza-som.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco-monza-som.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco-monza-som.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco-monza-som.dtsi
@@ -289,6 +289,7 @@
 /* Ethernet/SGMII */
 &serdes0 {
 	phy-supply = <&vreg_l5a>;
+	vdda-0p9-supply = <&vreg_l4a>;

 	status = "okay";
 };
